DIAGNOSTIC: read back the CSID configuration, not just the CSIPHY one

WHY
---
For the CSIPHY it was verified that the 110 writes of the lane table land
(patch 0064). For the CSID not a SINGLE one had been verified.

And it is a gap that matters: if CSI2_RX_CFG0 does not keep what was written to
it -for example because it is written before the block comes out of reset- the
receiver would be listening to a different PHY, or with a different lane count,
and EVERYTHING else would be consistent with what was measured: the PHY hears
the sensor, the CSID answers on registers, and not a packet arrives.

Read on stop, next to the counters from 0072:

    CSI2_RX_CFG0    lanes, lane mapping, which PHY it listens to, PHY type
    CSI2_RX_CFG1    ECC correction, MISR, virtual channel mode
    RDI_CFG0        format, data type, virtual channel, enable
    RDI_CTRL        start/stop command

What is expected for the front camera, with 4 lanes on CSIPHY1:

    rx_cfg0 = 0x00132103    (4-1) | 0x3210<<4 | 1<<20 | 0<<24
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-gen2.c	2026-08-17 12:44:26.193495273 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-gen2.c	2026-08-17 12:44:26.210457264 +0200
@@ -469,6 +469,25 @@
 					 csid->id, diag_pkts, diag_crc,
 					 diag_pkt_hdr0, diag_pkt_hdr1,
 					 diag_bytes_rdi0);
+
+				/*
+				 * Y RELEER LA CONFIGURACION.
+				 *
+				 * Del CSIPHY se comprobo que las 110 escrituras
+				 * aterrizan; del CSID no se habia comprobado
+				 * ninguna. Si CSI2_RX_CFG0 no guarda lo que se
+				 * le escribio -por ejemplo porque se escribe
+				 * antes de que el bloque salga del reset- el
+				 * receptor estaria escuchando a otro sitio y
+				 * todo lo demas seria coherente con lo medido.
+				 */
+				dev_info(csid->camss->dev,
+					 "csid%d config: rx_cfg0=0x%08x rx_cfg1=0x%08x rdi_cfg0=0x%08x rdi_ctrl=0x%08x\n",
+					 csid->id,
+					 readl_relaxed(csid->base + CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0),
+					 readl_relaxed(csid->base + CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG1),
+					 readl_relaxed(csid->base + CSID_RDI_CFG0(i)),
+					 readl_relaxed(csid->base + CSID_RDI_CTRL(i)));
 			}
 
 			__csid_configure_rdi_stream(csid, enable, i);
